  waits for an operation that takes a long time

  relies on a process being friendly.
  (infinite loop -> unfriendly, simply holding the processor for the rest of life.)

preemptive scheduling->
  the kernel stops a process at any time.
  kernel has a timer running, when timer is up

  windows 3.1
